RE","language":"en","shortDescription":{"text":"The MITRE Common Weakness Enumeration"},"taxa":[{"id":"328","guid":"dc1e99c1-c57b-5af0-85a4-9ad3bfac9c82","shortDescription":{"text":"Use of Weak Hash"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The product uses an algorithm that produces a digest (output value) that does not meet security expectations for a hash function that allows an adversary to reasonably determine the original input (preimage attack), find another input that can produce the same hash (2nd preimage attack), or find multiple inputs that evaluate to the same hash (birthday attack)."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"none"}},{"id":"330","guid":"80cf7ee1-5a29-5fb4-a2f1-701272abf9b7","shortDescription":{"text":"Use of Insufficiently Random Values"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The product uses insufficiently random numbers or values in a security context that depends on unpredictable numbers."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"}},{"id":"78","guid":"de860c32-bc93-5e70-89d7-0877e5abaefb","shortDescription":{"text":"Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')"},"fullDescription":{"text":"The product constructs all or part of an OS command using externally-influenced input from an upstream component, but it does not neutralize or incorrectly neutralizes special elements that could modify the intended OS command when it is sent to a downstream component."},"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"}}]}]}]}
